     "text": "```json\n{\"count\": 0, \"rationale\": \"Every non-foothold step is reachable, and the target is an OR over codeRepo:collection, dbReplica:collection, shareMount:collection and vaultRead:collection. No single block cuts all of them. (1) codeRepo:collection is reached via monitoringHost:lateralMovement, whose parents are configSecret:credentialAccess (fed directly by the vpnGateway foothold), ssoLogin:authenticate and dbLogin:authenticate. Blocking configSecret leaves ssoLogin, and blocking ssoLogin leaves configSecret, so monitoringHost survives. (2) If monitoringHost itself is blocked, codeRepo and vaultRead are still reached via jumpHost:lateralMovement <- dbLogin (mailClient AND configSecret). Both of those have foothold parents. (3) shareMount:collection is reached via secretsManager <- vpnSession AND ssoLogin, which gives a further independent route. (4) Every upstream step either has an entry-foothold parent or alternatives, e.g. tokenCache is fed directly by supplychain and ciRunner by three footholds. So no single step is a single point of failure.\"}\n```"
    }
